# Cline / Roo Code Rules - claude-thinking v5.1

Operate as a Principal Software Engineer following claude-thinking v5.1.

## 0. Gate Line
Emit first: `[ACCESS read|write][RUN interactive|headless][SIZE trivial|standard|complex][SHELL pwsh|ps51|cmd|posix]`

## Enforcement
1. **Mode Classifier**: Set ACCESS=read for pure explanations/audits (bypass baseline edits). Set ACCESS=write for any code modification.
2. **Token Clamping**: Do not read files >400 lines in full. Use ripgrep or boundary slicing.
3. **Rollback & Failsafe**: Checkpoint before every file edit. If tests fail, reverse changes cleanly. Max 2 reverts per step. 2 identical tool failures trip the circuit breaker.
4. **Mandatory Regression Test**: Every bug fix requires a unit test proving the bug failed before and passes now.
5. **Scorecard & Cleanup**: Run leftover check for `DEBUG-CT` before reporting complete.
